(Title) Tj
T*
(Intensive nurse-administered disease management versus routine care in inflammatory bowel) Tj
T*
(disease: randomized trial of patient-centered outcomes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Specialist nursing coordination plays a vital role in IBD management, yet rigorous) Tj
T*
(evidence on intensive nurse-led models remains limited. This randomized trial compared two) Tj
T*
(care approaches in 98 patients with IBD newly commencing advanced immunosuppressive) Tj
T*
(therapies. Participants were randomly assigned \(intensive arm n=50, control arm n=48\) to) Tj
T*
(either weekly nurse contact including scheduled telephone check-ins and in-person clinic) Tj
T*
(visits, or standard care involving baseline education only. The primary outcome was change) Tj
T*
(in an integrated disease-burden assessment score at 12 weeks. Both groups showed) Tj
T*
(improvement in disease-burden measures; however, the intensive-contact arm demonstrated) Tj
T*
(significantly greater score reductions. At 12 weeks, substantially more intensive-contact) Tj
T*
(participants achieved clinically meaningful treatment response. By 52-week follow-up, the) Tj
T*
(intensive-contact group maintained superior disease-control trajectories and higher rates) Tj
T*
(of disease remission. Adverse event profiles were comparable between arms. Results support) Tj
T*
(intensive nurse-led management for improving disease trajectories and outcomes in patients) Tj
T*
(initiating advanced IBD therapies.) Tj
ET
